{"created": "2026-11-11T20:54:29.817840+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-11T20:54:29.996769+00:00", "id": 24146136, "conceptrecid": "24146135", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146136", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146135", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24146136", "metadata": {"title": "rism-anon", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146136", "publication_date": "2026-11-11", "description": "<p>This repository finds anonymous music manuscripts in RISM that open with the same melody as a work RISM attributes to a named composer, and offers the pairs to RISM's editors. Matches are candidates, not attributions.</p><p>Status: pilot, claimed, not peer reviewed.</p><p>A claimed re-run on the 1 Oct 2026 export found that 13,696 of 138,817 anonymous records with a usable incipit open with the same 12 notes as attributed records by exactly one composer. No match has been checked by a person.</p><p>The counts come from RISM's monthly open-data export, which is under CC BY 3.0. The data are RISM's. They are not redistributed here, and the export is not in this archive.</p><p>Directed by Ahraz Arifuddin</p><p>Researched and verified by different model families across Gemini, Claude, Grok, OpenAI, and Muse</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Arifuddin, Ahraz", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["attribution", "digital-humanities", "foundation0", "music-manuscripts", "musicology", "rism"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/rism-anon", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v1.0.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/rism-anon"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "apache2.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24146135"}}]}}, "title": "rism-anon", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24146136", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/r